<p>The most common tactic involves inflating costs based on floor elevation. Transporters may quote a base price assuming a ground-floor pickup or delivery, then demand substantial premiums if your residence is on a third or higher floor, especially if the building lacks functioning elevators. Similarly, "long carry" charges are frequently weaponized.</p>
